---
import Tool from '../../layouts/Tool.astro';
import SysexBuilder from '../../components/SysexBuilder.astro';
---

<Tool slug="sysex" description="Build MIDI System Exclusive messages with manufacturer IDs, Universal SysEx presets, Roland and XOR checksums and 7-bit encoding, then copy or send them.">
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Assemble System Exclusive messages byte by byte: pick a manufacturer, add a header and data, and let the builder
    frame the message, compute the checksum, and flag bytes that don't fit in 7 bits. Copy the result as hex, decimal
    or a C array, or send it to a device.
  </Fragment>
  <SysexBuilder level={2} />
  <p slot="after" class="note-small">
    Manufacturer IDs are a selection from the MIDI Association's
    <a href="https://midi.org/sysexidtable">SysEx ID table</a>. Header and data layouts are device-specific: check
    your instrument's MIDI implementation chart. To decode a message you received, paste it into the
    <a href="/tools/decoder/">message decoder</a>.
  </p>
</Tool>
